{{also|OOPS}}
==English==

===Etymology===
A presumably 'natural' exclamation, attested in writing since 1921. Related to or a variation of {{m|en|whoops}} (itself attested since 1933). A shortening of {{m|en|whoops-a-daisy}}, {{m|en|whoopsie-daisy}}, or ''oops-a-daisy'', which in turn is a mispronunciation of {{m|en|ups-a-daisy}} or {{m|en|upsy-daisy}}.

